        "# 🌍 Climate Data Fetcher\n",
        "\n",
        "**Notebook 1 of 3: Fetching Hourly Climate Data for 11 UK Cities**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 📋 Purpose\n",
        "This notebook fetches hourly climate data from [Meteostat](https://dev.meteostat.net/python/) for 11 UK cities over the last 10 years (2014-2024).\n",
        "\n",
        "## 🎯 Cities Included\n",
        "| City | Region | Latitude | Longitude | Notes |\n",
        "|------|--------|----------|-----------|-------|\n",
        "| London | South East | 51.5074° N | 0.1278° W | Mild winters, warm summers |\n",
        "| Manchester | North West | 53.4808° N | 2.2426° W | Cooler, wetter |\n",
        "| Birmingham | West Midlands | 52.4862° N | 1.8904° W | Continental influence |\n",
        "| Leeds | Yorkshire | 53.7995° N | 1.5490° W | Cooler northern climate |\n",
        "| Glasgow | Scotland | 55.8642° N | 4.2518° W | Maritime, cooler |\n",
        "| Edinburgh | Scotland | 55.9533° N | 3.1883° W | Cooler, windier |\n",
        "| Cardiff | Wales | 51.4816° N | 3.1790° W | Maritime, mild |\n",
        "| Belfast | Northern Ireland | 54.5973° N | 5.9301° W | Maritime, cool |\n",
        "| Bristol | South West | 51.4545° N | 2.5879° W | Mild, wet |\n",
        "| Newcastle | North East | 54.9783° N | 1.6177° W | Coolest, most northerly mainland |\n",
        "| Lerwick | Shetland Islands | 60.1550° N | 1.1456° W | Far north, maritime, cool and windy |\n",
        "\n",
        "## 📊 Data Fetched\n",
        "- **Time Period:** 2014-01-01 to 2024-12-31 (10 years)\n",
        "- **Granularity:** Hourly\n",
        "- **Parameters:** Temperature, Humidity, Wind Speed, Pressure, Sunshine, Precipitation\n",
        "\n",
        "## 🔗 Sources\n",
        "- [Meteostat Python Library](https://dev.meteostat.net/python/)\n",
        "- Data sources: NOAA, ECAD, and other meteorological services\n",
        "- License: [CC BY 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Install required dependencies\n",
        "# Note: meteostat is the primary library for fetching climate data\n",
        "!pip install meteostat pandas numpy tqdm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Import libraries\n",
        "from meteostat import Point, Hourly\n",
        "from datetime import datetime\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import os\n",
        "from tqdm import tqdm\n",
        "import warnings\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 📍 City Metadata\n",
        "Load the list of UK cities with their coordinates and metadata."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Load city metadata from CSV\n",
        "metadata_path = '../data/climate/uk_cities_metadata.csv'\n",
        "cities_df = pd.read_csv(metadata_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display the cities\n",
        "display(cities_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert to list of dictionaries for easier access\n",
        "cities = cities_df.to_dict('records')\n",
        "print(f'\\nTotal cities to fetch: {len(cities)}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🏗️ Climate Data Fetcher Class\n",
        "A reusable class for fetching hourly climate data from Meteostat."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class ClimateDataFetcher:\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Fetches hourly climate data from Meteostat for specified locations.\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Parameters\n",
        "    ----------\n",
        "    cache_dir : str, optional\n",
        "        Directory to cache raw API responses, by default 'data/climate/cache'\n",
        "    start_date : datetime, optional\n",
        "        Start date for data fetching, by default Jan 1, 2014\n",
        "    end_date : datetime, optional\n",
        "        End date for data fetching, by default Dec 31, 2024\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def __init__(self, cache_dir: str = '../data/climate/cache', \n",
        "                 start_date: datetime = None, \n",
        "                 end_date: datetime = None):\n",
        "        self.cache_dir = cache_dir\n",
        "        os.makedirs(cache_dir, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Set default date range (last 10 years)\n",
        "        if start_date is None:\n",
        "            self.start_date = datetime(2014, 1, 1)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            self.start_date = start_date\n",
        "            \n",
        "        if end_date is None:\n",
        "            self.end_date = datetime(2024, 12, 31, 23, 59)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            self.end_date = end_date\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def fetch_hourly_data(self, city_name: str, lat: float, lon: float) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Fetch hourly climate data for a single city.\n",
        "        \n",
        "        Parameters\n",
        "        ----------\n",
        "        city_name : str\n",
        "            Name of the city (used for caching and file naming)\n",
        "        lat : float\n",
        "            Latitude of the city\n",
        "        lon : float\n",
        "            Longitude of the city\n",
        "        \n",
        "        Returns\n",
        "        -------\n",
        "        pd.DataFrame\n",
        "            DataFrame with hourly climate data and the following columns:\n",
        "            - time: datetime\n",
        "            - temp: air temperature (°C)\n",
        "            - dwpt: dew point temperature (°C)\n",
        "            - rhum: relative humidity (%)\n",
        "            - wspd: wind speed (m/s)\n",
        "            - wdir: wind direction (°)\n",
        "            - pres: atmospheric pressure (hPa)\n",
        "            - tsun: sunshine duration (minutes)\n",
        "            - precip: precipitation (mm)\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        location = Point(lat, lon)\n",
        "        data = Hourly(location, self.start_date, self.end_date)\n",
        "        data = data.fetch()\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Add city name for reference\n",
        "        if data is not None and not data.empty:\n",
        "            data['city'] = city_name\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return data\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def save_to_csv(self, df: pd.DataFrame, city_name: str) -> str:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Save DataFrame to CSV file.\n",
        "        \n",
        "        Parameters\n",
        "        ----------\n",
        "        df : pd.DataFrame\n",
        "            DataFrame containing climate data\n",
        "        city_name : str\n",
        "            Name of the city (used for filename)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        Returns\n",
        "        -------\n",
        "        str\n",
        "            Path to the saved CSV file\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        # Create output directory if it doesn't exist\n",
        "        output_dir = '../data/climate'\n",
        "        os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Create filename\n",
        "        filename = f'{city_name.lower().replace(" ", "_")}_2014-2024_hourly.csv'\n",
        "        filepath = os.path.join(output_dir, filename)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Save to CSV with datetime formatting\n",
        "        df.to_csv(filepath, index_label='time')\n",
        "        \n",
        "        print(f'✅ Saved {len(df)} hourly records to {filepath}')\n",
        "        return filepath\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def fetch_and_save_city(self, city: dict) -> str:\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        Fetch data for a city and save to CSV.\n",
        "        \n",
        "        Parameters\n",
        "        ----------\n",
        "        city : dict\n",
        "            Dictionary containing city metadata with keys:\n",
        "            - city_name: str\n",
        "            - latitude: float\n",
        "            - longitude: float\n",
        "        \n",
        "        Returns\n",
        "        -------\n",
        "        str\n",
        "            Path to the saved CSV file\n",
        "        \"\"\"\n",
        "        city_name = city['city_name']\n",
        "        lat = city['latitude']\n",
        "        lon = city['longitude']\n",
        "        \n",
        "        print(f'📍 Fetching data for {city_name} ({lat}°N, {lon}°W)...')\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Fetch data\n",
        "        df = self.fetch_hourly_data(city_name, lat, lon)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        if df is None or df.empty:\n",
        "            print(f'⚠️  No data returned for {city_name}')\n",
        "            return None\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Print summary\n",
        "        print(f'   📊 Data range: {df.index.min()} to {df.index.max()}')\n",
        "        print(f'   📈 Records: {len(df)}')\n",
        "        print(f'   🌡️  Temp range: {df["temp"].min():.1f}°C to {df["temp"].max():.1f}°C')\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Save to CSV\n",
        "        filepath = self.save_to_csv(df, city_name)\n",
        "        return filepath"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 🚀 Fetch Data for All Cities\n",
        "Now let's fetch data for all 11 UK cities. This may take 30-60 minutes depending on Meteostat's rate limits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Initialize the fetcher\n",
        "fetcher = ClimateDataFetcher()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Print date range\n",
        "print(f'📅 Fetching data from {fetcher.start_date} to {fetcher.end_date}')\n",
        "print(f'🌍 Total cities: {len(cities)}')\n",
        "print('=' * 60)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Fetch and save data for all cities\n",
        "# Using tqdm for progress bar\n",
        "\n",
        "saved_files = []\n",
        "failed_cities = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for city in tqdm(cities, desc='Fetching climate data'):\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        filepath = fetcher.fetch_and_save_city(city)\n",
        "        if filepath:\n",
        "            saved_files.append(filepath)\n",
        "    except Exception as e:\n",
        "        print(f'❌ Error fetching {city["city_name"]}: {str(e)}')\n",
        "        failed_cities.append(city['city_name'])\n",
        "\n",
        "print('=' * 60)\n",
        "print(f'✅ Successfully fetched and saved: {len(saved_files)}/{len(cities)} cities')\n",
        "if failed_cities:\n",
        "    print(f'❌ Failed cities: {failed_cities}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Display list of saved files\n",
        "if saved_files:\n",
        "    print('\\n📁 Saved files:')\n",
        "    for i, filepath in enumerate(saved_files, 1):\n",
        "        print(f'{i}. {os.path.basename(filepath)}')\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Calculate total records\n",
        "    total_records = 0\n",
        "    for filepath in saved_files:\n",
        "        df = pd.read_csv(filepath, parse_dates=['time'], index_col='time')\n",
        "        total_records += len(df)\n",
        "        \n",
        "    print(f'\\n📊 Total hourly records across all cities: {total_records:,}')\n",
        "    print(f'📅 Expected records (11 cities × 10 years × 365.25 days × 24 hours): {11 * 10 * 365.25 * 24:,.0f}')\n",
        "    completion_pct = (total_records / (11 * 10 * 365.25 * 24)) * 100\n",
        "    print(f'✅ Data completion: {completion_pct:.1f}%')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Quick validation: Check one city's data\n",
        "if saved_files:\n",
        "    sample_file = saved_files[0]\n",
        "    sample_df = pd.read_csv(sample_file, parse_dates=['time'], index_col='time')\n",
        "    \n",
        "    print(f'\\n🔍 Sample data from {os.path.basename(sample_file)}:')\n",
        "    display(sample_df.head())\n",
        "    \n",
        "    print('\\n📊 Basic statistics:')\n",
        "    display(sample_df.describe())\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Check for missing values\n",
        "    print('\\n🔎 Missing values:')\n",
        "    display(sample_df.isnull().sum())"
      ]
    },
